       POSIX.1‐2024.

HHIISSTTOORRYY
       POSIX.1‐2001.

       Kernel  support  first  appeared in Linux 2.5.60; the underlying system
       call is called ffaaddvviissee6644().  Library support has  been  provided  since
       glibc 2.2, via the wrapper function ppoossiixx__ffaaddvviissee().

       Since  Linux  3.18, support for the underlying system call is optional,
       depending on the setting of  the  CCOONNFFIIGG__AADDVVIISSEE__SSYYSSCCAALLLLSS  configuration
       option.

       The  type  of  the  _s_i_z_e  argument  was changed from _s_i_z_e___t to _o_f_f___t in
       POSIX.1‐2001 TC1.

