       The contents of  the  kernel  buffer  cache  can  be  cleared  via  the
       _/_p_r_o_c_/_s_y_s_/_v_m_/_d_r_o_p___c_a_c_h_e_s interface described in pprroocc(5).

       One  can obtain a snapshot of which pages of a file are resident in the
       buffer cache by opening a file, mapping it with mmmmaapp(2), and  then  ap‐
       plying mmiinnccoorree(2) to the mapping.

BBUUGGSS
       Before  Linux  2.6.6,  if _s_i_z_e was specified as 0, then this was inter‐
       preted literally as "zero bytes", rather than  as  meaning  "all  bytes
       through to the end of the file".

